                        "sense_id": "c46cb95b-b89f-379c-ba73-ba937b8b770a",
                        "entry_id": "abbf86c4-25cb-3146-ab76-cbee86d985eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tool used to remove concrete."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4039d26c-c58c-44e4-bba3-8912cd30b9cb",
                                "sense_id": "c46cb95b-b89f-379c-ba73-ba937b8b770a",
                                "text": "Concrete floors and walls can be mechanically decontaminated by removing the contaminated surface layer (1 to 2 inches) using surface grinders, spallers, or pneumatic drills."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e4b7447-1417-4386-9388-958afdbf17cf",
                                "sense_id": "c46cb95b-b89f-379c-ba73-ba937b8b770a",
                                "text": "The concrete spaller system contains a hydraulic power supply system and the spaller device. The spaller device, as shown in Figure 19, basically consists of a hydraulic cylinder, a push rod, and a bit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fdec7ec-f1db-44ed-a052-99d7da936749",
                                "sense_id": "c46cb95b-b89f-379c-ba73-ba937b8b770a",
                                "text": "The concrete spaller is a device which has been developed specifically for removing concrete surfaces by Pacific Northwest Laboratory (PNL)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "33998d81-a83c-3dd2-aa5c-112a625c9e9b",
                        "entry_id": "abbf86c4-25cb-3146-ab76-cbee86d985eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who breaks down stone into smaller pieces."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05eb93b2-12f4-47e3-883b-43fb8ebf0f6e",
                                "sense_id": "33998d81-a83c-3dd2-aa5c-112a625c9e9b",
                                "text": "In 1919, the weekly margin above the living wage for the \"all others\" item was 6s., though the spallers then received 9s. a week margin and the millhands only 3s."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80aff240-2850-4aec-b57b-abf94e2d51f9",
                                "sense_id": "33998d81-a83c-3dd2-aa5c-112a625c9e9b",
                                "text": "After them came men called spallers, who broke the rock down into smaller lumps, generally about three inches across, with sledgehammers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d20b39a-3399-430e-ae3c-abe1e64853a8",
                                "sense_id": "33998d81-a83c-3dd2-aa5c-112a625c9e9b",
                                "text": "Many days have I spent watching the female spallers breaking the stones. In the year 1899 I started to work at Dolcoath but there were not many spallers there then as they had just put in crushers which were worked by steam."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
